0000:                   ********************************************************************
0000:                   * IOMan - NitrOS-9 Level 2 I/O Manager module
0000:                   *
0000:                   * $Id$
0000:                   *
0000:                   * Edt/Rev  YYYY/MM/DD  Modified by
0000:                   * Comment
0000:                   * ------------------------------------------------------------------
0000:                   *          ????/??/??  ???
0000:                   * NitrOS-9 2.00 distribution.
0000:                   *
0000:                   *  13      2002/04/30  Boisy G. Pitre
0000:                   * Fixed a long-standing bug in IOMan where the I$Detach routine would
0000:                   * deallocate the V$STAT area.  This is because the V$USRS offset on the
0000:                   * stack, where the temporary device table entry was being built, contained
0000:                   * zero.  I$Detach wouldn't bother to do a lookup to see if it should
0000:                   * release the memory if this value was zero, so we now force I$Detach to
0000:                   * do the lookup no matter the V$USRS value.
0000:                   *
0000:                   *  13r2    2002/12/31  Boisy G. Pitre
0000:                   * Made more source changes, found discrepancy in value of POLSIZ in
0000:                   * certain areas, fixed. Also added 6809 conditional code for future
0000:                   * integration into OS-9 Level Two.
0000:                   *
0000:                   *  13r3    2003/03/04  Boisy G. Pitre
0000:                   * Conditionalized out Level 3 code.
0000:                   *
0000:                   *  13r4    2003/04/09  Boisy G. Pitre
0000:                   * Fixed bug where wrong address was being put in V$STAT when driver's
0000:                   * INIT routine was called.
0000:                   *
0000:                   *  13r5    2004/07/12  Boisy G. Pitre
0000:                   * Fixed bug where device descriptor wasn't being unlinked when V$USRS > 0
0000:                   * due to the value in X not being loaded.
0000:                   
0000:                            nam   IOMan
0000:                            ttl   NitrOS-9 Level 2 I/O Manager module
